{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788264272,"nonce":"X7RPuXNEPepVRK/Wg+sjia5I6cA=","title":"Doctor coverage is computable, so the mod should compute it: work_coverage in the digest, and a roster-change repair","message":"Lesson `[[one-doctor-is-zero-doctors]]` rescoped as code, per Evan's ruling of 2026-09-01 that **a deterministic finding goes in the mod, not in a note** (DESIGN decisions log; `postmortem.md` step 5 and the ladder's mod rung, now MANDATORY).\n\n## The evidence this exists to answer\n\nM1 run `m1-20260831`. The only pawn with Doctor enabled was Table, and **Table was the first casualty**. `Alert_NeedDoctor` fired *after* he was down. Both colonists who died died of **blood loss, untended** — not of the manhunter crow that downed them. One doctor is zero doctors the moment that doctor is the patient.\n\nThe lesson has been written since the run and, until this session, was cited by no checklist at all. That is the argument for the rung: prose that nobody loads at the moment it matters does not prevent anything.\n\n## Why this qualifies for the mod rung\n\nEvery input is already published by the observation surface: work-type enabled flags, skill levels, and `WorkGiver` eligibility. There is no judgement branch — \"how many pawns can currently doctor\" is arithmetic over state the mod already reads. Per the ladder, a response computable end to end from published state does not get to stop at a lower rung.\n\n## Scope\n\n**`DigestVerb.cs` — publish a `work_coverage` block.** Per essential work type, the count of pawns with it enabled AND capable (not just assigned — a pawn with the work type enabled but incapable of it is the same trap one level down). Doctor's floor is **2**, and the floor is what the digest compares against, so under-coverage is visible at every read rather than discovered in an emergency. State the floor for each essential type and the reasoning for the number.\n\n**`PawnManageVerbs.cs` — the roster-change repair.** On a roster change (death, downing, recruitment, a colonist leaving), enable Doctor on the best remaining capable pawn. This is the second tenant of the procedure rung beside post-raid (`cc8988c`). Report per-pawn refusals rather than silently picking nobody — an incapable roster is a real answer and the agent needs to see it.\n\nRead the game's own source for capability (`WorkTypeDef`, `Pawn.WorkTypeIsDisabled`, `WorkGiver` eligibility) and cite file + member, never line numbers.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `digest` publishes `work_coverage` with, per essential work type, enabled-and-capable count against a stated floor; Doctor's floor is 2.\n- The block distinguishes \"enabled but incapable\" from \"capable\" — prove it with a pawn who has the work type enabled and is incapable of it.\n- A roster change that drops Doctor coverage below the floor causes the repair to enable Doctor on the best remaining capable pawn, journalled as an act.\n- When NO capable pawn remains, the verb reports that refusal explicitly rather than succeeding with nobody assigned.\n- `checklists/` colony-start item 7 (\"Doctor coverage means TWO\") shrinks to confirming the mod's read, and `[[one-doctor-is-zero-doctors]]` keeps only the WHY.","files":null}]}